y're coming from a different group. The SI gets its money the old fashioned (criminal) way, through smuggling drugs, weapons, and people. They also have a major backer, the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> In my games I run a &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; so even though I'm running a Vampire game, there will be elements of other supernatural groups out there. In older editions the Technocracy didn't really care about vampires. Vampires weren't terribly powerful and they kept up a Masquerade. This put them fairly low on the Technocracy's hit list, and the general consensus was, &quot;We'll wipe them out when we win the Ascension War.&quot; That changes when Ravnos woke up. The Technocracy was completely shocked at how powerful Ravnos was. They began looking into vampires more and found out that there were a lot more vampires than they had previous assumed, and also apparently there were at least 12 more of god-like vampires, and possibly others who were even stronger.<br /> <br /> So the Technocracy decided that vampires had to be dealt with. They didn't have the manpower or resources to go after vampires though. They considered actively getting governments in on killing vampires, but quickly dismissed the idea. If the existence of vampires became official knowledge within many governments, eventually that knowledge would percolate up into the general public, and the public learning the truth about vampires is the last thing they wanted to see. So they began helping to set up an organization of people who would go after vampires, religious fundamentalists, actual vampire hunting organizations and then largely sat back and provided funding and the occasional bit of assistance. There are some links between the SI groups in North America and Europe, but it's mostly limited to sharing information and a bit of funding.<br /> <br /> I did include the destruction of the Tremere's Vienna Chantry in my games. That one was the result of a direct Technocratic attack rather than the Second Inquisition. The Technocracy decided to move against vampires and chose to start with the Tremere. Due to the Tremere's origins, the Technocracy know where they were located and had some ideas about their defenses and also believed that, thanks to their magical roots, they were the most dangerous vampire clan. They did have some misunderstandings though, believing that the Tremere were a cornerstones of vampiric society and if they took them out, the Camarilla would collapse. They also thought they could kill Tremere in Vienna and by doing so that would kill or disable most of clan Tremere, which is what they think happened to Clan Ravnos when they killed Ravnos.<br /> <br /> Things didn't work out very well. They did destroy the Chantry and killed quite a few vampires, but many of the elders managed to escape. In the end the Technocracy is of the opinion that the Vienna Chantry raid was a complete disaster. They lost too many resources and personnel and the results weren't anywhere near what they were hoping for. The Technocracy isn't going to engage in another similar show of force anytime soon. Of course the Kindred don't realize that.<br /> <br /> So ultimately I tend to keep the Second Inquistion fully separate from various governments, and I tend to really downplay and largely ignore any sort of governmental vampire group, because again, that's not really a direction I want my vampire games to go, with the government going after them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fantastic write-up and I give you a huge amount of props for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T13:00:15-07:00","id":1537352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1321827-hunters-hunted-ii-and-the-second-inquisition?p=1537344#post1537344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. One of my problems with the Second Inquisition, as written, is that it entirely changes the dynamic of Vampire games into one that's way less workable FOR Vampire games. If the government - or multiple governments - are all in on the SI, that means the consequences for being found are too big. If a PC gets discovered by the SI, the player might as well hand in their character sheet then and there. Because they're just screwed, in a way the players can't really wriggle out of, unless their characters skip town. (Which, of course, has functionally the same outcome as them dying; unless the whole Coterie gets found out, and every player is willing to switch to a Fugitive style game, they're out of the picture).<br /> <br /> Hunter organizations being small, underfunded operations works very well for street-level or higher games. Dangerous enough to be an existential threat, but not overwhelming enough that you can't deal reasonably deal with it. Inquisition cells can be cleared out, and SAD agents can disappear. There might be problems down the line, like if other cells come knocking or the disappeared agents turn into Martyrs, X-Files Agent Mulder style. But a Vampire PC could, possibly, go back to their unlife if they're thorough enough. Being discovered by hunters doesn't turn into a cascading failure state that renders the Chronicle itself (or at least that PC's part in it) non-viable.<br /> <br /> If you WANT there to be such high stakes, cool, that's your prerogative. But that probably shouldn't be the baseline of how a Vampire game works. At best, dealing with a global anti-Vampire conspiracy coming down on you should be the climax of a Chronicle. (Similar to the entire city turning against you in <i>VtM: Bloodlines</i>. Once you hit that point, you're in the endgame.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the disappointment of the Second Inquisition book for me as I expected there to be a lot of details that just weren't there. I also expected there to be government infighting, a variety of goals, and a sense of just what the limits of their funding as well as resources were.<br /> <br /> Instead, we got &quot;light grenades.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}